2. GPU firmware (not part of this repository)

The PSP, DMCUB and SMU firmware files come from linux-firmware (LICENSE.amdgpu, Copyright (C) 2024 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.). That licence allows redistribution in binary form only, requires the copyright notice and permission notice to be reproduced in the documentation, and forbids reverse engineering, decompilation and disassembly. It also subjects the software to United States export laws.

For that reason this repository contains no firmware, no C arrays generated from firmware, and no disassembly of it. The tools in tools/ (gen_psp_fw_header.py, gen_dmub_fw_header.py, parse_psp_fw.py) read the container headers that the Linux driver documents and turn a file the user fetched into a local, git-ignored header. Anyone who distributes a kext built with such a header is responsible for reproducing the AMD notice and permission notice (see LICENSE.amdgpu in linux-firmware) with it.

3. Other projects

RedNavi is not derived from NullMoth, NootedRed or LegacyRed and contains no code from them. The architecture follows the approach NullMoth shows for NVIDIA; the Linux and FreeBSD drivers were read as references for behaviour.

`RedNavi/mes_v11_api_def.h` is `drivers/gpu/amd/include/mes_v11_api_def.h` from the Linux kernel (Copyright 2022 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., MIT licence, the notice is in the file): the MES firmware's command frame layouts.

RedNavi/mmhub_regs.h is generated by tools/gen_gc_regs.py from the AMD mmhub_3_0_0 register headers (MIT licence, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.), like RedNavi/gc_regs.h.
